  "body": "What happens: `carry_turn` (crates/app/src/stock_sim_carry.rs, around line 116) refuses a stock carry onto any machine whose kind is not `Mill`, and the refusal text `CARRY_MACHINE_REFUSAL` reads \"a part flip or sub-spindle hand-off is not supported yet on a lathe or mill-turn machine\". Two setups on a sinker EDM linked \"Same as\" (or flipped) get that text, which names the wrong machine kind. Seen while pinning PR #1131 (#541): `GenerateOperation` on a Sinker Burn in Setup2 returns \"... carrying the machined stock from setup 'Setup1' into setup 'Setup2': a part flip or sub-spindle hand-off is not supported yet on a lathe or mill-turn machine\".\n\nThe refusal itself is right (the column lattice carries milled bodies only, nothing is cut on a guess); only the wording is wrong. Pinned today by `a_carry_onto_the_sinker_is_refused_by_name_before_any_burn` in crates/app/tests/sinker_burn_held.rs, which asserts the constant, not its wording.\n\nExpected: the refusal names the target machine's kind (e.g. \"... is not supported yet on a sinker EDM machine\"), via `machine.label()` or similar, keeping the constant's prefix so existing `contains` checks hold.\n\nDone means: a carry onto a non-mill setup names that machine's kind in the refusal; a test pins it for a sinker EDM and for a lathe.\n",
